---
<Base {...meta} jsonld={jsonld}>
<main id="main">
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="hero__layout">
        <div class="hero__copy">
          <div class="eyebrow">For bank and credit union leadership teams</div>
          <h1 class="display-title hero__title">Marketing measurement and market analysis.</h1>
          <p class="subhead">Measure marketing, compare branch markets, test acquisition footprints, or add senior marketing leadership.</p>
          <div class="actions">
            <a class="btn" href="https://cal.com/pauldrago/20-min-intro-call" data-cal-link="pauldrago/20-min-intro-call" data-cal-namespace="20-min-intro-call" data-cal-config='&#123;"layout":"month_view","useSlotsViewOnSmallScreen":"true","theme":"auto"&#125;'>Book a call</a>
            <a class="text-link" href="#decisions">Compare the services</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <nav class="decision-nav" aria-label="Financial services decisions">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="decision-nav__inner">
        <a href="#measurement">Measurement</a>
        <a href="#branch">Market expansion</a>
        <a href="#acquisition">Acquisition analysis</a>
        <a href="#fractional">Fractional CMO</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </nav>

  <hr class="section-divider"/>

  <section class="section" id="decisions">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 class="display-title section-title">Four ways I work with financial institutions.</h2>
      <p class="section-intro">Choose a defined analysis project or bring in senior marketing leadership. Each engagement starts with the reports and data the institution already uses.</p>

      <div class="router">
        <div class="router__group-label">Decision projects</div>
        <div class="router__row router__row--visible" id="measurement">
          <div>
            <div class="router__service">Marketing Measurement Reset</div>
            <h3 class="router__question">Show what acquisition spend produced after account opening.</h3>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="router__body">For institutions that can report account openings but cannot show which accounts stayed open, funded, or justified the spend.</p>
            <p class="router__fit"><strong>You receive:</strong> agreed measurement definitions, a spend-to-retained-account and funded-balance model, and a board-ready reporting view.</p>
            <p class="router__data">Uses digital account opening reports, core data, CRM exports, campaign spend, and funded balance views.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="router__visual" aria-hidden="true"><div class="router__visual-label">Spend to retained accounts, illustrative</div><div class="spend-flow"><div class="spend-flow__line"><span>Spend</span><div class="spend-flow__track"><div class="spend-flow__fill" style="width:100%"></div></div><span class="spend-flow__value">100%</span></div><div class="spend-flow__line"><span>Opened</span><div class="spend-flow__track"><div class="spend-flow__fill" style="width:100%"></div></div><span class="spend-flow__value">100%</span></div><div class="spend-flow__line"><span>90 days</span><div class="spend-flow__track"><div class="spend-flow__fill" style="width:55%"></div></div><span class="spend-flow__value">55%</span></div><div class="spend-flow__line"><span>One year</span><div class="spend-flow__track"><div class="spend-flow__fill spend-flow__fill--accent" style="width:41%"></div></div><span class="spend-flow__value">41%</span></div></div></div>
            <a class="router__link" href="/marketing-measurement-reset">View measurement service</a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="router__row router__row--visible" id="branch">
          <div>
            <div class="router__service">Branch and Market Expansion Analysis</div>
            <h3 class="router__question">Compare markets before committing to a branch plan.</h3>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="router__body">For leadership teams comparing new markets, branch locations, or expansion priorities.</p>
            <p class="router__fit"><strong>You receive:</strong> a market scorecard, competitor and deposit-share view, customer-geography comparison, CRA and fair-access review points, and a reusable assumptions model.</p>
            <p class="router__data">Uses FDIC, NCUA, Census, competitor footprint, customer geography, the latest CRA performance evaluation, current assessment areas, and institution fair-lending and branch-policy inputs.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="router__visual" aria-hidden="true"><div class="router__visual-label">Market scorecard, illustrative</div><div class="market-grid"><div class="market-grid__cell"></div><div class="market-grid__cell market-grid__cell--live"></div><div class="market-grid__cell"></div><div class="market-grid__cell"></div><div class="market-grid__cell market-grid__cell--live"></div><div class="market-grid__cell"></div><div class="market-grid__cell"></div><div class="market-grid__cell"></div><div class="market-grid__cell"></div><div class="market-grid__cell market-grid__cell--branch"></div><div class="market-grid__cell market-grid__cell--live"></div><div class="market-grid__cell"></div><div class="market-grid__cell market-grid__cell--live"></div><div class="market-grid__cell"></div><div class="market-grid__cell market-grid__cell--live"></div><div class="market-grid__cell"></div><div class="market-grid__cell market-grid__cell--live"></div><div class="market-grid__cell"></div><div class="market-grid__cell"></div><div class="market-grid__cell"></div><div class="market-grid__cell market-grid__cell--live"></div></div></div>
            <a class="router__link" href="/branch-market-expansion-analysis">View branch analysis service</a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="router__row router__row--visible" id="acquisition">
          <div>
            <div class="router__service">Acquisition and Footprint Analysis</div>
            <h3 class="router__question">Test the market case for an acquisition target.</h3>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="router__body">For teams evaluating whether a target adds attractive deposits, fills a market gap, or creates footprint and local-brand risk.</p>
            <p class="router__fit"><strong>You receive:</strong> a deposit and market profile, footprint-overlap view, documented retention assumptions, and an executive decision brief.</p>
            <p class="router__data">Uses branch-level deposits, market overlap, local growth, customer geography, product mix, and retention assumptions.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="router__visual" aria-hidden="true"><div class="router__visual-label">Footprint overlap, illustrative</div><div class="overlap-visual"><div class="overlap-visual__circle"></div><div class="overlap-visual__circle overlap-visual__circle--target"></div><div class="overlap-visual__note">Overlap is duplicated branches</div></div></div>
            <a class="router__link" href="/acquisition-footprint-analysis">View acquisition analysis service</a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="router__group-label router__group-label--embedded">Embedded leadership</div>
        <div class="router__row router__row--visible" id="fractional">
          <div>
            <div class="router__service">Fractional CMO, Regulated Financial Services</div>
            <h3 class="router__question">Add senior marketing leadership without a full-time hire.</h3>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="router__body">For banks and regulated financial-services companies that need an experienced operator to lead the function.</p>
            <p class="router__fit"><strong>You receive:</strong> priorities, finance and board reporting, agency and vendor direction, a weekly and monthly working rhythm, and leadership for the internal team.</p>
            <p class="router__data">Designed for work that spans marketing planning, budget management, compliance, board reporting, and coordination with outside partners.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="router__visual" aria-hidden="true"><div class="router__visual-label">Reporting cadence, illustrative</div><div class="cadence"><div class="cadence__bar" style="height:48px"></div><div class="cadence__bar" style="height:60px"></div><div class="cadence__bar cadence__bar--live" style="height:74px"></div><div class="cadence__bar" style="height:66px"></div><div class="cadence__bar" style="height:84px"></div><div class="cadence__bar cadence__bar--live" style="height:100px"></div></div><div class="cadence-labels"><span>M1</span><span>M2</span><span>M3</span><span>M4</span><span>M5</span><span>M6</span></div></div>
            <a class="router__link" href="/fractional-cmo-financial-services">View fractional CMO service</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="section-divider"/>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 class="display-title section-title">What happens after the first call.</h2>
      <div class="process">
        <div class="process__step">
          <div class="process__title">Define the question.</div>
          <div class="process__body">Clarify the budget, market, acquisition, measurement, or leadership issue.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="process__step">
          <div class="process__title">Review the current reports.</div>
          <div class="process__body">Start with the reports the institution already trusts, uses, or questions.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="process__step">
          <div class="process__title">Agree on definitions.</div>
          <div class="process__body">Definitions, dates, exclusions, attribution, balance logic, and source conflicts.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="process__step">
          <div class="process__title">Build and test the model.</div>
          <div class="process__body">Tie each input and assumption to the question the leadership team needs answered.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="process__step">
          <div class="process__title">Hand off the work.</div>
          <div class="process__body">The institution keeps the model, definitions, source logic, and reporting format.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="process-note">Defined projects end with a reusable model and reporting the institution can keep using. Fractional CMO work continues through an agreed meeting and reporting rhythm with the internal team, finance, compliance, and outside partners.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="section-divider"/>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="not-agency">
        <div>
          <h2 class="display-title section-title">Where I fit.</h2>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="section-intro section-intro--flush">This work sits between financial analysis, growth planning, and senior marketing leadership. It is designed for institutions that need a usable model or an experienced operator.</p>
          <div class="no-list">
            <div><strong>Measurement</strong><span>Spend, retained accounts, funded balances</span></div>
            <div><strong>Market analysis</strong><span>Branches, deposits, competitors, customer geography</span></div>
            <div><strong>Executive leadership</strong><span>Priorities, reporting, teams, agencies, vendors</span></div>
            <div><strong>Outside scope</strong><span>Creative production, events, standalone media buying</span></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="section-divider"/>

  <section class="closing-band" id="the-call">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="closing-band__grid">
        <div>
          <h2 class="display-title section-title">Tell me what the institution is trying to decide.</h2>
          <p class="subhead">In 20 minutes, we will define the question, identify the reports already available, and determine whether there is enough information for useful work.</p>
          <div class="actions">
            <a class="btn" href="https://cal.com/pauldrago/20-min-intro-call" data-cal-link="pauldrago/20-min-intro-call" data-cal-namespace="20-min-intro-call" data-cal-config='&#123;"layout":"month_view","useSlotsViewOnSmallScreen":"true","theme":"auto"&#125;'>Book a call</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <aside class="call-note" aria-label="What to bring to the call">
          <div class="call-note__label">What to bring</div>
          <p>Send the report, market, target, or operating question you want to discuss. A clean data set is not required for the first conversation.</p>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>
</Base>
